  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "26.11.0 - fidelity release: XFA forms, HTML in and out, PDF/A and text.\n\nNew: LinkAnnotation.Hyperlink; UpdateAppearances on underline and squiggly annotations; ChoiceField.SetValue; StructureElement.Remove; Page.ProcessSpecialSymbols; ExtGState.FillOpacity and StrokeOpacity; PdfFunction.ClampInput and ClampOutput; ImageLoadException, raised for image bytes no decoder can read instead of an image that silently draws nothing.\nXFA: dynamic forms render and convert to standard forms closer to their design - load-time scripts run before the pages are painted, fields and text draws continue across content areas and pages, captions, check boxes and radio buttons take the sizes they declare, and a converted form lists exactly the fields its template defines, filled from their data bindings.\nHTML: HTML-to-PDF and HTML import read more real-world pages - stylesheet selectors and exclusions, list markers, preformatted blocks that clip, form controls at their CSS sizes, bordered, spanning and block-laid table cells; PDF-to-HTML ships the fonts widget appearances use, keeps right-to-left text in its order and keeps page text out of PNG backgrounds; SVG import handles nested svg viewports, symbols drawn through use, text-only foreignObject and SVG images in data URIs.\nPDF/A and fonts: conversions repair TrueType and Type 1 font dictionaries (CharSet, CIDToGIDMap, encodings), restate soft masks and trim oversized Indexed palettes; the standard Asian faces are found by name; font fallback prefers installed broad-coverage faces and never puts a fixed-pitch face in place of a proportional one.\nText: replacements keep right-to-left lines shaped and in visual order and move the rest of their line by the width they gained; sub- and superscripts set on a segment draw as scripts; auto-tagging reads raised marks, list labels and suffixes on the lines they belong to; the table absorber finds column boundaries and spanned cells inside ruled tables.\nSigning and redaction: SHA-1 PKCS#1 and PKCS#7 signatures are written as their handlers define, a nested signature field is found by its full name, and a signing update keeps the form dictionary's entries; an applied redaction draws its overlay appearance and removes its own mark, and JPEG images in CMYK, palette or Lab colour stay lossless in their own colour space.\nAlso: CMYK colours are written as CMYK; generated layouts read correctly on rotated pages; rendering fixes for clip paths, thin strokes and indexed images; faster saves of dense pages, duplicate-stream optimization and XFA field reads.\n\nFull release notes: https://github.com/aspose-pdf-foss/Aspose.PDF-FOSS-for-.NET/releases/tag/v26.11.0",
